From 26ad779433db2285a31e89bbffeda2382b3f5b86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:47:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NSSplitView: -adjustSubviews asks about every subview, the
 last one too

-adjustSubviews asked the delegate's -splitView:shouldAdjustSizeOfSubview:
about every subview but the last, which always took whatever space was
left: a trailing pane (an inspector, a button bar) could not keep its size
as the split view grew or shrank.  And the subviews that did adjust were
given their share of the whole span, not of what the fixed ones left, so
the last one made up the difference.

On macOS 15, with three subviews and the delegate saying only the middle
one adjusts, growing the split view leaves the first and the last at
their sizes and gives the middle all of the change; the delegate is asked
about all three.  With only the last one adjusting, the first two keep
theirs and the last takes the change.

So -adjustSubviews asks about every subview.  When it is not restoring
autosaved proportions, a subview not to adjust keeps its size and those
to adjust share what is left in proportion to the sizes they had, the last
of them taking the rounding; when none is to adjust, or the fixed ones no
longer fit, every subview adjusts, as without a delegate.  Restoring
autosaved proportions is unchanged.

Tests/gui/NSSplitView/adjustSubviewsDelegate.m checks this both ways
round; it passes with the change, and without it 6 of its 16 checks fail.
The rest of the NSSplitView tests pass as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
